Subject: [PATCH] ipa: nxp: neo: apply requested sensor frame durations

The open Neo IPA advertises FrameDurationLimits but does not apply it to
sensor blanking or exposure. A 1080p50 request consequently stays at the
sensor default of 30 fps despite negotiating 50 fps GStreamer caps.

Retain frame-duration requests per frame, clamp them to sensor timing
limits, bound AGC and manual exposure, and send VBLANK through the existing
sensor-control path. Register VBLANK with the existing delayed-control
handler using the sensor properties, and apply it before exposure controls.
Report the delayed sensor blanking in metadata. Carry camera startup
controls into the first IPA request, preserving per-request overrides.
Zero duration values retain the mode defaults. Keep hardware ISP processing.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Raven Contributors <raven@localhost>
